    "size_pt": 26
  },
  {
    "text": "Motivation",
    "x": 20,
    "y": 156,
    "width": 402,
    "height": 18.07633333333333,
    "size_pt": 42
  },
  {
    "text": "1. Text-based references can drift between similar objects. Coordinate-only grounding lacks explicit identity tracking.",
    "x": 22,
    "y": 412,
    "width": 398,
    "height": 23.311555555555554,
    "size_pt": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "2. A model may correctly analyze object A, then silently point to object B. This reasoning-to-answer misalignment breaks reliable visual grounding.",
    "x": 22,
    "y": 452,
    "width": 398,
    "height": 23.311555555555554,
    "size_pt": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "Key Insight: Persistent Identity",
    "x": 448,
    "y": 156,
    "width": 373,
    "height": 18.07633333333333,
    "size_pt": 42
  },
  {
    "text": "View 0",
    "x": 452,
    "y": 191,
    "width": 148,
    "height": 10.329333333333333,
    "size_pt": 24
  },
  {
    "text": "obj_01",
    "x": 459,
    "y": 213,
    "width": 65,
    "height": 9.898944444444442,
    "size_pt": 23
  },
  {
    "text": "View 1",
    "x": 665,
    "y": 191,
    "width": 148,
    "height": 10.329333333333333,
    "size_pt": 24
  },
  {
    "text": "obj_01",
    "x": 672,
    "y": 213,
    "width": 65,
    "height": 9.898944444444442,
    "size_pt": 23
  },
  {
    "text": "From isolated grounding to persistent anchors",
    "x": 452,
    "y": 328,
    "width": 365,
    "height": 12.481277777777777,
    "size_pt": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "• Spatial references are usually isolated annotations, without explicit identity tracking during reasoning.",
    "x": 454,
    "y": 350,
    "width": 360,
    "height": 22.91644444444444,
    "size_pt": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "• PinCoT binds each entity to a name, ID, view and point. Later steps reuse the same ID.",
    "x": 454,
    "y": 389,
    "width": 360,
    "height": 22.91644444444444,
    "size_pt": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "• Our insight: visual anchors act as persistent reasoning variables, making each step traceable to visual evidence.",
    "x": 454,
    "y": 428,
    "width": 280,
    "height": 34.37466666666666,
    "size_pt": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "QR\nPLACEHOLDER",
    "x": 762,
    "y": 441,
    "width": 44,
    "height": 13.772444444444442,
    "size_pt": 16
  },
  {
    "text": "PAPER / CODE",
    "x": 750,
    "y": 475,
    "width": 68,
    "height": 7.31661111111111,
    "size_pt": 17
  },
  {
    "text": "Our Method: RoboPIN / PinCoT",
    "x": 20,
    "y": 494,
    "width": 801,
    "height": 19.797888888888885,
    "size_pt": 46
  },
  {
    "text": "We propose PinCoT, which pins every reasoning step to visual evidence through persistent identity-aware anchors.\nRoboPIN learns this representation through SFT, CoT-SFT and process-supervised RFT / GRPO.",
    "x": 24,
    "y": 699,
    "width": 793,
    "height": 24.553333333333327,
    "size_pt": 30
  },
